{"body": "Decomposition of 27 Indian winner windows (25 case records plus BEL and both shipyards; screener TTM P/E, split-adjusted prices): log(price multiple) = log(EPS multiple) + log(P/E multiple). Median share of the log-return from rerating = 37%. Long runs (9+ years: Bajaj Finance, Page, Astral, Pidilite, Titan, Eicher, Balkrishna, APL Apollo, Deepak, Tata Elxsi, Garware, Alkyl) had a median rerating share of ~36%; EPS compounding did most of the work. Short runs (≤5.5 years: KPIT 62%, Cochin 88%, HAL 66%, Mazagon 53%, CDSL 50%, Dixon 42%, Kaynes 29%, Trent 14%) had a median of ~51%. Rerating-heavy cases (>50% from P/E: Cochin, HAL, KPIT, Symphony, Balkrishna, Tata Elxsi, Mazagon, CDSL) are a median ~54% below their ATH on 19 Nov 2026. HAL (−14%), whose EPS kept rising, is the exception. Earnings-heavy cases (≤30%: Trent, Page, Titan, Avanti, Eicher, Caplin, La Opala, Polycab, Kaynes) had mixed outcomes: Titan and Eicher are near highs, while La Opala and Kaynes are down 60%+. Where they fell, it was because growth slowed, not because a pure multiple was undone. Rule: when more than half of a gain is multiple, the gain is fragile; check whether EPS can carry the price if P/E returns to its median. Caveat: windows start at lows, which inflates P/E expansion.", "confidence": "verified", "created": "2026-11-19T19:59:02Z", "data": {"long_run_median": "~36%", "median_pe_share": "37%", "method": "log decomposition, TTM P/E", "n": 27, "short_run_median": "~51%"}, "date": "2026-11-19", "id": "insight:india-mb-twin-engine-base-rate", "links": [{"rel": "part_of", "to": "insight:twin-engine"}, {"rel": "about", "to": "case_study:indian-shipyards-2020-2025"}, {"rel": "about", "to": "case_study:kpit-technologies-2020-2024"}, {"rel": "about", "to": "case_study:hal-2020-2024"}, {"rel": "about", "to": "case_study:tata-elxsi-2009-2022"}, {"rel": "about", "to": "case_study:balkrishna-industries-2009-2024"}, {"rel": "about", "to": "case_study:titan-2009-2026"}, {"rel": "about", "to": "case_study:trent-2020-2024"}], "sources": ["https://www.screener.in/"], "tags": ["india", "multibagger", "base-rate", "valuation", "twin-engine"], "title": "India multibaggers: ~2/3 of return is EPS, ~1/3 rerating (long runs); ~1/2 rerating (short runs)", "type": "insight", "updated": "2026-11-19T19:59:02Z", "version": 1}
{"body": "Same-method promise scores for four US mid-cap industrial / building-products companies (last 6 earnings calls each, Jul-2025 to Nov-2026; Motley Fool transcripts, 8-K Ex 99.1 press releases where no transcript was found: WTS Q3-25, SSD Q2-26, LECO Q2-25 and Q2-26). Weighted delivery (credit, specificity-weighted): US-WTS 100.0% (n=12), US-AOS 65.9% (n=18), US-SSD 79.4% (n=7), US-LECO 88.5% (n=6). Sector pattern: explicit company-level margin and growth ranges are met or beaten (pooled margin 92.9%, revenue/growth 70.7%), because US managements guide conservatively and raise; misses cluster in China / international sub-lines (A. O. Smith), capex forecasts and plant ramps (pooled capacity 50.0%). A. O. Smith cut its FY2026 guide three times (Jan-26 items score withdrawn). Most FY2026 guidance is pending and n is small (6-18 scored per company). SAC (pts vs leave-one-out peer medians): US-WTS +15.3, US-AOS -35.3, US-SSD -7.0, US-LECO -11.5. Use: base rates for credibility-generated paper calls (thesis tags credibility-generated, us). Provisional. Research, not advice.", "confidence": "single-source", "created": "2026-11-22T17:39:47Z", "data": {"adjustment_rule": "p0 = leave-one-out pooled STRICT delivery rate (specificity-weighted share 'delivered'; partly=0) of the other 3 peers in the promise's category (all-category peer rate if <8 peer promises in that category). p = clip(p0 + N/(N+20) x SAC/100, 0.05, 0.95), N = company's scored promises, SAC in points (credit basis: delivered 1, partly 0.5; categories with n<5, or with <2 peers having data, pooled). P(base) = p0.", "as_of": "2026-11-22", "base_rates_leave_one_out": {"US-AOS": {"_all": {"n": 25, "p0_pct": 82.1}, "capacity": {"fallback_all": true, "n": 3, "p0_pct": 82.1}, "margin": {"fallback_all": false, "n": 10, "p0_pct": 100.0}, "other": {"fallback_all": true, "n": 5, "p0_pct": 82.1}, "revenue_growth": {"fallback_all": true, "n": 7, "p0_pct": 82.1}}, "US-LECO": {"_all": {"n": 37, "p0_pct": 71.4}, "cap